Z||000007||Monkeyman||11-26-2001||03:22 AM||||Fieros have been my favorite car for almost 20 years.  Three years after the Fiero became my favorite car, the Mk III Supra became my 2<sup>nd</sup> favorite car.  (Mk III Supras came out in '86.)  I wouldn't be defecting at all.  Toyotas are some of the most reliable cars out there and I need reliability.  If I ever got rid of the Fiero for a Supra, it would only be until I could afford another Fiero.  As it is, I can't afford a Supra right now so the point is moot.  I'm hoping to get a Supra in the spring.  If there are those that will shun me because they think I defected to the import side, so be it.  Those of you who have been here a while know of my infatuation with the Fiero and know that I just want to add another neat car to my stable.  If you're my friend now, you will be no matter what kind of car I drive be it a Fiero or a riced out Honda Accord (no chance of that, though).  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||mshill||11-26-2001||05:09 PM||||I bought an 85 Conquest right out of college.  what a wonderful car to drive.  I took it on a 1000 mile run to So Cal down I-5 and averaged 90 mph,  felt like I was going 25 mph the entire trip, an it was probably the most comfortable car I have ever driven.<P>Our apartment complex suffered a flood in 1987.  With the ECM under the seat it never quite recovered.  Great car.<BR>||||reg||1
